From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 20:32:45 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: keep one Wi-Fi local fastpath session per flow

The Wi-Fi local fastpath adds a session when a listed application
sends a packet. It did so for each packet of a flow whose session had
no Wi-Fi mark. Such a flow filled all session slots, and a flow that
started later found no free slot.

A flow now has at most one session.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/arht_wifi_lo.c |    9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/arht_wifi_lo.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/arht_wifi_lo.c
@@ -797,6 +797,12 @@ static void wifi_lo_add_ety(struct sk_bu
 		dst_hold(dst);
 
 	spin_lock_bh(&wifi_lo_lock);
+	/* The static key turns on from a work item, and two CPUs can miss
+	 * the lookup of the hook at the same time.
+	 */
+	if (wifi_lo_find_by_port(th->source, th->dest))
+		goto unlock;
+
 	for (i = 0; i < WIFI_LO_MAX_NUM; i++) {
 		lo = &wifi_lo_ety[i];
 		/* Skip both live slots and slots whose previous occupant is
@@ -834,6 +840,7 @@ static void wifi_lo_add_ety(struct sk_bu
 		added = true;
 		break;
 	}
+unlock:
 	spin_unlock_bh(&wifi_lo_lock);
 
 	if (!added) {
@@ -978,6 +985,8 @@ static unsigned int wifi_lo_nf_hook_loca
 			return NF_STOLEN;
 		}
 		rcu_read_unlock();
+		if (lo)
+			return NF_ACCEPT;
 	}
 
 	if (wifi_lo_app_match(current->comm))
